.TH _PRINTF 3 "January 2025" "Custom printf"
.SH NAME
_printf \- formatted output conversion
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "main.h"
.sp
.BI "int _printf(const char *" format ", ...);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The
.B _printf
function produces output according to a format string. It supports the following conversion specifiers:
.TP
.B %c
Print a single character.
.TP
.B %s
Print a string.
.TP
.B %%
Print a literal percent sign.
.TP
.B %d, %i
Print a signed integer in base 10.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of characters printed (excluding the null byte).
.SH EXAMPLES
To print "Hello, 42!":
.sp
.B _printf("Hello, %d!\\n", 42);
